module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Simplicial.ZariskiRingedTopos

/-!
# A covering of the top travels along a continuous functor with no terminal object

`Stacks.Sheaves.LocalizedPullback.coversTop_map` carries a family covering the final object
along a continuous functor `u : D ⥤ C`, assuming that `u` takes a terminal object of `D` to a
terminal object of `C`. The total Zariski site of a simplicial scheme has no terminal object —
an object `(n, W)` receives one arrow from `(m, V)` for each map `⦋n⦌ ⟶ ⦋m⦌` of the simplex
category, and there are several — so that form of the lemma does not apply to it.

The terminal object is not needed. `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop` quantifies
over all objects, and at an object `A` of `C` it is enough to have *some* arrow from `A` into
the image of `u`: the image of the covering sieve of the target of that arrow is a covering
sieve, its pullback along the arrow is a covering sieve of `A`, and that pullback is contained
in the sieve generated by the image family, since `Sieve.ofObjects` depends only on the source
of an arrow. This file proves that form and specialises it to the total Zariski site, where the
hypothesis holds because every `(m, V)` maps to `(m, ⊤)` and `(m, ⊤)` is the image of `(m, ⊤)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.coversTop_map_of_coversTop_obj`: the image of a family covering the top
  covers the top, for a continuous functor whose family of images covers the top — that is,
  `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.CoversTop` is transitive along a continuous functor.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.coversTop_map_of_forall_exists_hom`: the image of a family covering the
  top covers the top, for a continuous functor into whose image every object of the target site
  admits an arrow. This is the case of the previous one in which the image family generates the
  maximal sieve, and it is the form the total Zariski site satisfies; a site whose objects are
  only *covered* by objects mapping into the image — the small étale site of an algebraic space
  inside a category fibred in groupoids representable by it — needs the previous one.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SimplicialScheme.coversTop_zariskiPullback`: the degreewise inverse images
  of a family covering the top of the total Zariski site of `U` cover the top of the total
  Zariski site of `V`, for a morphism of simplicial schemes `f : V ⟶ U`.

## Implementation notes

Continuity enters exactly as in `Stacks.Sheaves.LocalizedPullback.coversTop_map`, through
`CategoryTheory.CoverPreserving.of_isContinuous`: Mathlib's `Functor.IsContinuous` asks only
that restriction along the functor preserve sheaves, and that already gives preservation of
covering sieves in the direction needed here.

**What this is for, and what it does not supply.** Quasi-coherence of a sheaf of modules on a
site is equivalent to the existence of *one* family covering the top on whose members the module
has a global presentation, with no terminal object and no typeclass hypotheses
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_iff_coversTop_hasGlobalPresentation`). So for
Stacks 07TI on the total Zariski site — the pullback of a quasi-coherent module along a morphism
of simplicial schemes is quasi-coherent — the covering half of the argument is this file: a
family `{W_i}` covering the top of `U_Zar` on which `F` is globally presented gives the family
`{f⁻¹W_i}` covering the top of `V_Zar`. What is still missing is the presentation half, namely
that `(f^*F)|_{f⁻¹W_i}` is the pullback of `F|_{W_i}` along the localized morphism of ringed
topoi of Stacks 04J0; that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.Hom.localizedPullbackToposSquare`, which is available only under
`[HasFiniteLimits]` on both sites, false here.

